{
  "schemaVersion": "omega-route-products/v1",
  "about": "Which hosted Omega product each gateway route belongs to (READINESS 3.13, lane 1.10b). A request is admitted only when its verified key names the route's product in the `products` claim: absent is 404 product_not_admitted, present only as paused refuses new work with 503 product_paused. `platform` routes are the ones every tab needs and answer any workspace admitted to at least one product. A route the gateway admits that no entry here covers is refused (default deny). A product list means the route serves each of them (the credential list is read by the Console and by Deployments). whilePaused: the writes a paused product still serves because they stop or decide work rather than start it; EE refuses an approve while its product is paused. When the route manifest (lane 1.3) lands, each of its routes takes the product of the longest prefix below as its `product` field, in the FA copy and the byte-identical EE copy.",
  "products": ["console", "sandboxes", "deployments", "studio_tab", "hub"],
  "routes": [
    { "prefix": "/workspace/capabilities", "product": "platform" },
    { "prefix": "/workspace/sandboxes", "product": "sandboxes" },
    {
